        "r": 273.1639899999999,
        "b": 663.38021
      },
      "content": "Baseplate-leveling worksheet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0307",
      "reading_order": 356,
      "section": "Install the baseplate using shims or wedges",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 144.004,
        "t": 656.6202099999999,
        "r": 419.61400000000015,
        "b": 645.38021
      },
      "content": "This procedure is applicable to cast iron and fabricated steel baseplates."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0308",
      "reading_order": 357,
      "section": "Install the baseplate using shims or wedges",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 144.004,
        "t": 642.3376599999999,
        "r": 546.1940000000002,
        "b": 619.09766
      },
      "content": "If  you use sleeve-type bolts, fill the bolt sleeves with packing material or rags to prevent grout from entering the bolt holes."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0309",
      "reading_order": 358,
      "section": "Install the baseplate using shims or wedges",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 144.004,
        "t": 616.96812,
        "r": 517.7339800000002,
        "b": 591.20812
      },
      "content": "Put the sets of  wedges or shims on each side of  each foundation bolt. The sets of  wedges should have a height of  between 0.75 in. (19 mm) and 1.50 in. (38 mm)."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0030",
